      "slug": "gram:gp-37",
      "steps_unavailable": "The point is a PARTICLE CHOICE (が or の marking the subject) that is licensed only INSIDE a noun-modifying / subordinate clause; the record states の in a main clause is an error. The op set carries no scope condition, so a step list of the shape [noun, append の] would license *私のパンを作った in a main clause. The safe half (append が) alone would misrepresent a point that exists to teach the の alternation.",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "spoken",
        "written"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-38",
      "steps_unavailable": "Invariable interrogative pronoun. The record's formation describes that どれ stands alone as a pronoun and takes が/を, and contrasts it with どの + noun; it names no base and no derivation, so there is nothing to build.",
      "nuance_tags": [],
      "usage_contexts": [
        "spoken",
        "written"
      ]
    },
    {
      "slug": "gram:gp-39",
